{
  "measured_on": "2026-11-14",
  "how": "Each tool's own test_examples were run live; every value appearing under a declared key, at any depth of the response, was typed and counted. Counts are pooled across tools in the same config file that wrap the same upstream field. Round 1 took the fields the live sweep reported; round 2 measured EVERY field each affected tool declares, because jsonschema reports only the first error per validation, so round 1 saw one bad field per tool and fixing it unmasked the next. Round 3 found one more field that round 2's pass had NOT seen: the same two LINCS examples returned pubchem_id as an integer minutes after returning it as a string, so a single live pass is a LOWER BOUND on the types a field holds, not the complete set.",
